"""
  |OMC_BTS:
  | ------------------------------------------------------------
  |  ne3s_activate -- Activates NE3S protocol for FBOX proxy, registers manager and starts NE3S session
  | ------------------------------------------------------------
  |  Usage: ne3s_activate
  |[<REREGISTER_INTERVAL>][<REGISTRATION_CREDENTIALS>][<MANAGER_IDENTITY>][<TLS>][-pnp][-ac][-passive][-port <PORT>]
  |
  |  <REREGISTER_INTERVAL>
  |    - reregister interval in days (default 10)
  |
  |  <REGISTRATION_CREDENTIALS>
  |    - registration credentials options:
  |
  |        -user <USER>
  |            - registration user name (option in bts-file: -REG_USER, default: wsuser)
  |
  |        -password <PASSWORD>
  |            - registration password (option in bts-file: -REG_PASSWORD, default: A0zY~rP#8Mx@)
  |
  |        -ca_pub_key <CA_PUB_KEY>
  |            - path to CA public key
  |
  |        -manager_cert <MANAGER_CERT>
  |            - path to manager certificate
  |
  |        -manager_priv_key <MANAGER_PRIV_KEY>
  |            - path to manager private key
  |
  |  <MANAGER_IDENTITY>
  |    - registration manager identity options:
  |
  |        -manager_id <MANAGER_ID>
  |            - manager id: common, hw, cm or ac (default: common)
  |                common fragments:
  |                    ConfigurationManagement,
  |                    AgentDiscovery,
  |                    FaultManagement,
  |                    PerformanceManagement,
  |                    SubscriberAndEquipmentTrace,
  |                    AuditTrail,
  |                    HardwareManagement,
  |                    SoftwareManagement,
  |                hw fragments:
  |                    HardwareManagement
  |                cm fragments:
  |                    ConfigurationManagement
  |                ac fragments:
  |                    AgentDiscovery
  |
  |        -vendor <VENDOR>
  |            - manager vendor (default: Nokia)
  |
  |        -manager_type <TYPE>
  |            - manager type (default: NMS)
  |
  |  <TLS>
  |    - option to enable/disable TLS on OAM link:
  |        -tls <FLAG>
  |            - 1: enable TLS, 0: disable TLS
  |
  |  -pnp
  |    - activate PlugAndPlay functionality, i.e. do not start registration and do not activate a session
  |
  |  -ac
  |    - activate PlugAndPlay with Auto Configuration manager only
  |
  |  -passive
  |    - work in PlugAndPlay passive mode, i.e. do not perform Ne Identification and unregister after receiving
  |      CCN with NeIdentificationResult
  |  -port <PORT>
  |    - connect to BTS port <PORT> (option in bts-file: -NE3S_BTS_PORT
  |      Can be 4 digits or asi or cu (default=8080, ASIR default=6080, CU default=8060).
"""
